# Git sync for wow-addons

Full workflow: **[GEMORDER-GUIDELINES.md](../../GEMORDER-GUIDELINES.md)**

Remote: https://github.com/Henrik8210/wow-addons.git (branch `main`).

WoW install path (always copy here after GemOrder/GemOrderTest changes):
`C:\Program Files (x86)\World of Warcraft\_anniversary_\Interface\AddOns\`

After completing meaningful work on GemOrder or GemOrderTest:

1. Commit all relevant changes with a clear message (why, not just what).
2. Push to `origin/main` unless the user asked not to push.
3. Bump `## Version:` in the relevant `.toc` when shipping a new release build.
4. Run `.\scripts\sync-gemordertest.ps1` so GemOrderTest matches the same version.
5. Copy the updated `GemOrder/` and `GemOrderTest/` folders to the WoW AddOns path so the user can `/reload` immediately.

Do not leave addon code only on disk in the repo — deploy to WoW and keep GitHub as source of truth.
